SYNOPSIS
        void log_error(string file, string err, int warn, int line)

DESCRIPTION
        Announce a compiler-time error (warn == 0) or warning (warn != 0)
        in the named file at the given line number.

        Whenever the LPC compiler detects an error or issues a warning,
        this function is called. It should at least log the error in a file,
        and also announce it to the active user.

        The diagnostic text starts with file:line:column and the severity.
        When source context is available, it includes the original source
        line and an underline. Columns are one-based display columns; tabs
        use eight-column stops. Include sites and macro definitions may
        appear as additional notes. The text may therefore contain several
        lines. The callback's arguments are unchanged.

        Some early lexer errors and diagnostics without retained source
        context provide only file:line. Excerpts and expansion notes are
        bounded; source capture is limited per compilation. The diagnostic
        still reports its message when optional context is unavailable.

HISTORY
        LDMud 3.2.8 added the 'warn' argument and the warnings in general.
        LDMud 3.6.5 added the 'line' argument.

SEE ALSO
